Alchemy isn't necessary. After the quest, the 175+ hp she'll have once
she's gathered a level will effectively be 350+ hp. And before the
quest, there's no need to have over 150 hp (esp. with an AC below
-25). Increased constitution might still pay out - might give extra
hitpoints when levelling or faster hitpoint recovery, but i'm only
guessing here. 

> > What should I genocide next - Disenchanters of Mind Flayers?

For disenchanters, it's easiest to have a backup not-enchanted weapon
you can swap in (like a silver sabre or rustproof +0 long sword).
Alternatively, a bunch of missiles can kill them from afar - but will
mess up enchanted missiles - and some powerful pets are capable of
handling them, too. There's no actual need to genocide them.

> Definitiely MMF, or better--if you bless the scroll--all 'h'. Use those
> wands of cancellation you have against 'R'.

Without knowing whether Vicky is a human or dwarf (which, alas, has
not been disclosed by the original poster) that's potentially
dangerous advice. Being lawful and having over 18 Dx, she _can_
certainly be a dwarf and would thus be required to burn two genocide
scrolls to get rid of brain-eaters.

> > I have a tub of grease - will a greased helmet keep the mind flayers off?
> 
> Not 100% and it wears off easily.

Until it wears off, it protects completely (although there might be an
extra case for non-protection if the helmet itself is cursed).
However, each tentacle hit - even if it would have been blocked by the
helmet - is a hit on the grease film and has 50% chance of dissolving
it, allowing the tentacles to get purchase on the next attack. 

One application of grease tends to protect from _one_ attack by a mind
flayer, and half an attack of a master mind flayer (the latter gets so
many attacks and has such a good chance to connect that it frequently
manages to dissolve the grease and successfully suck your brain in the
same round).

